{% assign pf = site.data.policy_feasibility %}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ '/assets/css/policy-feasibility.css' | relative_url | bust_file_cache }}">
<div
  id="policy-feasibility"
  class="pf-project pf-v2"
  data-pf-map="{{ '/assets/data/policy-feasibility/countries.geojson' | relative_url | bust_file_cache }}"
>
  <nav class="pf-stepnav" aria-label="Sections of this page">
    <ol>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-top"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">·</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Framework</span></a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-define"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">01</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Question</span></a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-scope"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">02</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Outside view</span></a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-trajectories"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">03</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Trajectories</span></a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-assess"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">04</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Inside view</span></a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="#pf-model"><span class="pf-stepnav-number">05</span><span class="pf-stepnav-label">Scenario</span></a>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <header id="pf-top" class="pf-intro pf-reveal">
    <p class="pf-caption">
      A companion to the research article
      <a href="{{ pf.article_url }}"><em>The politics of baselines: A political feasibility framework for energy and climate scenarios</em></a> ·
      Fornborg (2026), <em>Energy Research &amp; Social Science</em>
    </p>
    <p class="pf-intro-lead">
      Energy and climate scenarios often rely on assumptions about future policy developments that are highly contested. Despite this, they are rarely
      screened for political feasibility before they enter models. This page demonstrates how a set of plausible policy responses to the rapid growth
      of datacenter electricity demand in Sweden can be identified, screened for political feasibility and carried into a power system model.
    </p>
  </header>

  <figure class="pf-method pf-fw pf-reveal" aria-labelledby="pf-framework-title">
    <figcaption>
      <h2 id="pf-framework-title">The framework</h2>
      <p>
        Following Kahneman and Lovallo (1993) and Jewell and Cherp (2023), the framework combines an outside view with an inside view. The outside
        view allows a scoping of plausible policy trajectories through spatial and temporal comparison, while the inside view enables an assessment of
        the feasibility of trajectories informed by political economy and institutional theory.
      </p>
    </figcaption>
    <div class="pf-fw-grid">
      <p class="pf-fw-step pf-fw-s1" style="--pf-d: 0"><span>1</span> Outside view · scope</p>
      <p class="pf-fw-step pf-fw-s2" style="--pf-d: 4"><span>2</span> Inside view · compare</p>
      <p class="pf-fw-step pf-fw-s3" style="--pf-d: 6">Scenario use</p>

      <a class="pf-fw-sources" href="#pf-scope" style="--pf-d: 1">
        <span>Historical precedent and policy momentum</span>
        <span>Institutional practice and commitments</span>
        <span>Actor positions and stakeholder signals</span>
      </a>
      <svg class="pf-fw-arrow pf-fw-a1" style="--pf-d: 2" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M4 16h22m-6-6 6 6-6 6" />
      </svg>
      <a class="pf-fw-candidates" href="#pf-trajectories" style="--pf-d: 3">
        <strong>Candidate policy trajectories</strong>
        <ul>
          <li>Trajectory 1</li>
          <li>Trajectory 2</li>
          <li>Trajectory …</li>
        </ul>
      </a>
      <svg class="pf-fw-arrow pf-fw-a2" style="--pf-d: 4" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M4 16h22m-6-6 6 6-6 6" />
      </svg>
      <div class="pf-fw-dimensions" style="--pf-d: 5">
        <a href="#pf-assess"><strong>Feasibility dimensions</strong></a>
        <ul>
          {% for d in pf.dimensions %}
            <li>
              <a href="#pf-dimension-{{ d.id }}" title="{{ d.guide }}">{{ d.name }}</a>
            </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <svg class="pf-fw-arrow pf-fw-branch" style="--pf-d: 6" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M4 16h22m-6-6 6 6-6 6" />
      </svg>
      <div class="pf-fw-use" style="--pf-d: 7">
        <a href="#pf-model"><strong>Trajectories carried into modelling</strong><span>Baseline, sensitivity case or alternative future</span></a>
        <a href="#pf-assess"><strong>Documented rationale and disagreements</strong></a>
      </div>
      <p class="pf-fw-reuse" style="--pf-d: 8">Evidence from step 1 is reorganised and reused in step 2</p>
    </div>
    <p class="pf-caption pf-fw-source">Adapted from Fig. 2 in the article.</p>
  </figure>

  <section id="pf-define" class="pf-section pf-case-intro pf-reveal">
    <div class="pf-case-copy">
      <p class="pf-step-tag">The case</p>
      <h2><span class="pf-section-number">01</span> The policy question</h2>
      <p class="pf-question">{{ pf.scope.question }}</p>
      <p class="pf-caption">Sweden · Decisions in {{ pf.decision_period }} · Rules apply from 2028 · Time horizon {{ pf.model_horizon }}</p>
    </div>
    <img
      class="pf-case-illustration"
      src="{{ '/assets/images/policy-feasibility/datacenter-linework.png' | relative_url }}"
      alt=""
      width="1714"
      height="918"
      decoding="async"
    >
    <div class="pf-case-context">
      <figure>
        {% include policy-feasibility/tracker-map.liquid %}
        <figcaption>
          {{ site.data.policy_feasibility_context.metric }}.<br>
          Announced projects by {{ site.data.policy_feasibility_context.year }}.<br>
          <a href="{{ site.data.policy_feasibility_context.source_url | relative_url }}">Nordic datacenter tracker, high scenario</a>
          · {{ site.data.policy_feasibility_context.snapshot_date | date: '%-d %B %Y' }}
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <h3>Why the rules are contested</h3>
        <ul class="pf-contested">
          <li>
            If the announced datacenter projects in the high scenario of the
            <a href="{{ '/projects/datacenter-tracker/' | relative_url }}">Nordic datacenter tracker</a> are built, they would add about
            {{ site.data.policy_feasibility_scenarios.dc_load_twh.total | round }} TWh to Swedish electricity use by 2035, roughly a quarter of
            today’s use.
          </li>
          <li>
            New generation and grid capacity take time. Onshore wind needs municipal approval, and offshore wind and new nuclear take years to permit
            and build.
          </li>
          <li>How the cost is shared between developers, households, industry and taxpayers is a political question.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    {% include policy-feasibility/next.liquid href='#pf-scope' number='02' title='Look across places and time' %}
  </section>

  {% include policy-feasibility/outside.liquid %}

  <section id="pf-trajectories" class="pf-section pf-reveal">
    <p class="pf-step-tag">From the outside view</p>
    <h2><span class="pf-section-number">03</span> Define comparable trajectories</h2>
    <p class="pf-prose">{{ pf.derivation }}</p>
    {% include policy-feasibility/trajectory-cards.liquid %}
    <p class="pf-specification-note">{{ pf.specification_note }}</p>
    {% include policy-feasibility/next.liquid href='#pf-assess' number='04' title='Assess political feasibility' %}

    <figure
      class="pf-policy-doodle"
      aria-label="Hand-drawn diagram: adopted policy remains in place through 2035, marked with a check. Or, rising household electricity costs, public protest and pressure on industry could lead policy in different directions."
    >
      <div class="pf-policy-doodle-assumption">
        <svg class="pf-policy-doodle-wide" viewBox="0 160 773 460" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <image href="{{ '/assets/images/policy-feasibility/policy-doodle-handdrawn-blue-v4.png' | relative_url }}" width="2092" height="752" />
          <path d="M 552 550 Q 558 556 563 562 Q 574 547 585 531" fill="none" stroke="#526b7b" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
        </svg>
        <svg class="pf-policy-doodle-narrow" viewBox="0 160 742 460" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <image href="{{ '/assets/images/policy-feasibility/policy-doodle-handdrawn-blue-v4.png' | relative_url }}" width="2092" height="752" />
          <path d="M 552 550 Q 558 556 563 562 Q 574 547 585 531" fill="none" stroke="#526b7b" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" />
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="pf-policy-doodle-responses">
        <svg viewBox="773 160 1319 460" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <image href="{{ '/assets/images/policy-feasibility/policy-doodle-handdrawn-blue-v4.png' | relative_url }}" width="2092" height="752" />
        </svg>
      </div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  {% include policy-feasibility/assess.liquid %}

  {% include policy-feasibility/scenario.liquid %}

  <div class="pf-sources-footer">
    <h2>Article and supporting material</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="{{ pf.article_url }}">The politics of baselines: A political feasibility framework for energy and climate scenarios</a>. David
      Fornborg, <em>Energy Research &amp; Social Science</em>, 141 (2026), 104981.
    </p>
    <div class="pf-links">
      <a href="{{ '/projects/political-feasibility/evidence/' | relative_url }}">Sources and evidence</a
      ><a href="{{ '/projects/datacenter-tracker/' | relative_url }}">Nordic datacenter tracker</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script type="application/json" id="pf-case-data">
    {{ pf | jsonify | replace: '<', '<' }}
  </script>
</div>
